From: Marcin <91057909+mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:34:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix serving files after the path traversal fix

Platinum now keeps the "/" file root when joining it to the requested
path, so ServeFile gets "/<md5>/<name>" and every file request fails
with 404. Drop the leading slash before looking up the hash.

(cherry picked from commit 0d8b2f91b9939d1e31a838d9f46ca03394a57ce9)
---
 xbmc/network/upnp/UPnPServer.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/network/upnp/UPnPServer.cpp b/xbmc/network/upnp/UPnPServer.cpp
index d3e3ec0..47b6e23 100644
--- a/xbmc/network/upnp/UPnPServer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/network/upnp/UPnPServer.cpp
@@ -1459,8 +1459,12 @@ failure:
 NPT_Result CUPnPServer::ServeFile(const NPT_HttpRequest& request,
                                   const NPT_HttpRequestContext& context,
                                   NPT_HttpResponse& response,
-                                  const NPT_String& md5)
+                                  const NPT_String& requested_path)
 {
+  // Platinum joins the requested hash to the "/" file root
+  const NPT_String md5(requested_path.StartsWith("/") ? requested_path.SubString(1)
+                                                      : requested_path);
+
   // Translate hash to filename
   NPT_String file_path(md5), *file_path2;
   {
-- 
